      "reason": "One bug fix, not 118 retirements. The page for the 2004 USS Nimitz encounter had accumulated 234 alias slugs, 118 of which name entirely different events - the 1947 Kenneth Arnold sighting, the 1948 Mantell incident, the 1950 McMinnville photographs, the 1964 Socorro landing. Every one of those URLs was live and served the Nimitz article, so a reader following a link about Kenneth Arnold arrived at a 2004 carrier encounter. The aliases were emitted correctly from what the graph held against that node at the time; the graph has since been corrected and a build-time assertion now refuses an alias naming a live node the page does not cover. None of the 118 has a correct destination - those events have no pages - so they now 404, which is the honest answer and better than the wrong one they were giving. No page file was removed; these were never files. Assembler fbce99b added the assertion, content da6ac25 removed the aliases.",
      "decided_by": "anomalica/assembler, verified against production by anomalica/site",
      "retired": "2026-09-08",
      "how_to_reverse": "git revert the commit that removed them; the URLs resolve again on the next deploy."
